    <title>Problems</title>
    <text><table><thead><tr><th>Problem</th><th>Clinical status</th><th>Verification</th><th>Code</th><th>Provenance</th></tr></thead><tbody>
  <tr ID="problem-1">
    <td>Breathlessness and tightness across the chest on exertion for about two months, late in long nights of refereeing in hot arenas, easing within a few minutes of rest; never at rest; no fainting, palpitations, orthopnea or ankle swelling; cause under evaluation with a cardiology consultation</td><td>resolved</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>R06.09</td><td>S — Synthetic presenting problem anchored to his documented work as a referee; superseded at the consultation when stress testing showed no ischemia and the symptom was attributed to hypertensive heart disease.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-2">
    <td>Stage 2 hypertension found at a yearly fitness examination for his referee&apos;s license (164/100 and 160/98 mmHg), with left ventricular hypertrophy by voltage on the ECG; untreated; home readings to follow</td><td>resolved</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>I10</td><td>S — Synthetic diagnosis at intake; reclassified as hypertensive heart disease after the echocardiogram at the consultation.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-3">
    <td>Hypertensive heart disease without heart failure: concentric left ventricular hypertrophy (septum 13 mm, mass index 118 g/m2) with normal ejection fraction, grade 1 diastolic dysfunction, a mildly enlarged left atrium and an exaggerated blood pressure rise on exercise; no features of hypertrophic cardiomyopathy</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>I11.9</td><td>S — Synthetic diagnosis made at the cardiology consultation; not a claim about his real heart.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-4">
    <td>Coronary atherosclerosis found by coronary calcium scoring (Agatston score 186, about the 80th percentile for his age and sex), without angina and with no inducible ischemia on exercise stress echocardiography</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>I25.10</td><td>S — Synthetic diagnosis made at the cardiology consultation; not a retrospective diagnosis of the cause of his death, which is disputed.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-5">
    <td>Hypercholesterolemia: LDL 160 mg/dL, HDL 44 mg/dL, lipoprotein(a) not raised; no diabetes</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>E78.00</td><td>S — Synthetic diagnosis at intake.</td>
  </tr></tbody></table></text>

