    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Hypertensive heart disease (I11.9)</content>. Better, and symptom-free at full cards, but home readings of 134/84 mmHg are still above the target of 130/80 mmHg, which matters with left ventricular hypertrophy. [S]<list><item>Increase to losartan 100 mg with hydrochlorothiazide 25 mg each morning.</item><item>Basic metabolic panel in two weeks (lab slip given).</item><item>Keep drinking water between bouts, more on hot nights.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Coronary atherosclerosis (calcium score 186) (I25.10)</content>. On atorvastatin 40 mg for five weeks without side effects. [S]<list><item>Lipid panel at about nine weeks, at the preventive visit.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Clinic blood pressure, average of two seated readings</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>136/86 mmHg</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Home blood pressure monitoring (validated upper-arm cuff), readings sent weekly</td><td>Every day during titration; then a week before each visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Two-week average 134/84 mmHg</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Basic metabolic panel (sodium, potassium, creatinine, eGFR)</td><td>Two to four weeks after starting or changing an ARB or diuretic; then every six months</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Sodium 138, potassium 3.9 mmol/L, creatinine 1.06 mg/dL, eGFR 84; repeat two weeks after today&apos;s increase</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Lipid panel</td><td>Four to twelve weeks after starting a statin; then yearly</td><td>Due</td><td>At about nine weeks on atorvastatin</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Symptoms: exertional chest discomfort, breathlessness, palpitations, fainting</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>None at four full cards</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Stress testing or coronary imaging</td><td>For new or changed exertional symptoms; not for routine surveillance</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>No new symptoms</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Echocardiogram</td><td>At diagnosis of stage 2 hypertension or suspected hypertrophy; repeat in six to twelve months to judge regression</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Repeat six to twelve months after the first</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Weight, BMI and physical activity</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>74.0 kg; brisk walks most mornings</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Adherence and side effects (cough, edema, muscle aches, lightheadedness)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No missed doses; no cough, lightheadedness or muscle aches</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Return to work: refereeing, heat and hydration, warning symptoms, defibrillator at the venue</td><td>Before return to full exertion; then every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Cleared for full cards three weeks ago; water between bouts</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Financial strain and medicine cost</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Both medicines are generics he can afford</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Find the cause of the exertional breathlessness and chest tightness. Outcome by 2026-05-26: No inducible ischemia; symptoms from hypertensive heart disease with an exaggerated blood pressure response [S]</item><item>Blood pressure below 130/80 mmHg at home and in the clinic. In progress; target 2026-08-25 [S]</item><item>LDL below 70 mg/dL and at least 50% lower than at intake. In progress; target 2026-07-28 [S]</item><item>Keep refereeing full cards safely, without symptoms. In progress; target 2027-05-12 [S]</item><item>Regression of left ventricular hypertrophy on a repeat echocardiogram. In progress; target 2027-05-26 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: 2025 AHA/ACC/AANP/AAPA/ABC/ACCP/ACPM/AGS/AMA/ASPC/NMA/PCNA/SGIM Guideline for the Prevention, Detection, Evaluation and Management of High Blood Pressure in Adults (2025); 2023 AHA/ACC/ACCP/ASPC/NLA/PCNA Guideline for the Management of Patients With Chronic Coronary Disease (2023); 2026 ACC/AHA/AACVPR/ABC/ACPM/ADA/AGS/APhA/ASPC/NLA/PCNA Guideline on the Management of Dyslipidemia (2026); Eligibility and Disqualification Recommendations for Competitive Athletes With Cardiovascular Abnormalities: Task Force 6: Hypertension (2015); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, hypertension, hyperlipidemia and ischemic heart disease monographs (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Basic metabolic panel in two weeks. Preventive visit at the end of July with the lipid panel. Fifteen-week review in late August. Next scheduled visit 2026-07-28: periodic adult preventive visit and recheck after the sick visit. [S]</paragraph></text>

